Bubble Sort repeatedly compares two adjacent elements and swaps them if they are in the wrong order
Algorithm:
For ascending order:

Start from the first element.
Compare two adjacent elements.
If the left element is greater than the right element, swap them.
Continue comparing adjacent elements until you reach the end.
After one complete pass, the largest element moves to the end.
Repeat the same process for the remaining unsorted part.
Stop after n - 1 passes, or earlier if no swaps happen.

public static void bubbleSort(int[] arr) {

    int n = arr.length;

    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {

        for (int j = 0; j < n - 1 - i; j++) {

            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {

                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                arr[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}

Complexity:
Best:    O(n²)
Average: O(n²)
Worst:   O(n²)
Space:   O(1)


Optimized solution:
boolean swapped = false;

for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {

    swapped = false;

    for (int j = 0; j < n - 1 - i; j++) {

        if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
            int temp = arr[j];
            arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
            arr[j + 1] = temp;

            swapped = true;
        }
    }

    if (!swapped) {
        break;
    }
}
Complexity: BestCase : O(n)
